{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sandstone-fiendish-auk","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nRP-01 proposes replacing Rebar’s bespoke structured-output orchestration with authoritative Pydantic AI seams. The replacement is not behavior-preserving by default: historical bugs encode hard-won behavior around deterministic repair and extraction, refusal/truncation handling, retry and tool/request limits, per-operation output budgets, provider fallback, usage accounting, telemetry, and failure taxonomy. Before RP-01 can be approved or ticketized, reconstruct the behavioral contract from both ticket history and the existing test suite and exercise Pydantic AI 1.107.2 offline. A behavior may be preserved or intentionally changed, but no observed delta may be accidental or left to the implementer.\n\n## Plan\n- Deduplicate ticket-derived scenarios with behavioral cases from the structured runner, failure-matrix, budget, timeout, and agent-call seam test suites.\n- Record each scenario’s current observable behavior and its authoritative ticket/test evidence.\n- Extend the ignored local FunctionModel probe to exercise Pydantic AI 1.107.2 native output, prompted output, output retry, usage limits, FallbackModel predicates, provider errors, truncation/refusal, telemetry, and artifact-capture feasibility without live model calls.\n- Classify each scenario as preserve, intentionally change, or requiring an explicit maintainer decision; do not infer an invariant from the current implementation alone.\n- Record the resulting evidence and experiment outputs in the local `.joe-janitor/` recovery archive and summarize the decision matrix on this ticket.\n\n## Verification\nThis is an investigation task. The smallest sufficient tier is an in-process integration probe using the real Pydantic AI 1.107.2 Agent/FunctionModel/output/limits/hooks seams while mocking only provider transport. The oracle is the exact call count, request mode, accepted semantic output, exception class, usage/accounting fields, and captured telemetry for each predeclared scenario. Existing unit tests provide the current-Rebar side of the comparison.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deduplicated matrix maps every material ticket-derived and test-derived scenario to exact ticket aliases and test node or source locations.\n- [ ] The matrix states current Rebar behavior and observed Pydantic AI 1.107.2 behavior for each scenario.\n- [ ] Every outcome difference is labeled preserve, intentionally change, or explicit decision required; no difference is silently inherited from either implementation.\n- [ ] The offline probe executes the real Pydantic AI output/retry/fallback/limits/hook seams and records exact observable oracles without a live model call.\n- [ ] A concise RP-01 research note and the probe are stored beside the recovered janitor artifacts under `.joe-janitor/`.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records the artifact paths, probe command and result, scenario coverage totals, and the next unresolved behavior decision.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call","id":"dd5a-bdec-f9a1-4b76","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","recovery","research","pydantic"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Resolve RP-01 structured-output seam against historical behavior"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786906436801434001,"uuid":"dde6aef7-d081-44f5-8561-e706b963d400"}